'' '@f' and 'procptr( f )' over an overload set take the overload the TARGET type names -- an
'' initialiser, an assignment, an argument, byref-ness included -- as fbc does. Check records the
'' choice and types '@f' by it; lowering reads it (overload re-pick refactor, Phase 1).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/procaddr-target-overload.bas -o tests/codegen/procaddrtargetoverload.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/procaddrtargetoverload.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: double 1.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: long 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: double 2.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: byref2 3 4
